515	 * The newest request is the current one, so this reads newest-first. The node's BODY
516	 * is the oldest entry in its own thread — it is what the node was opened asking for —
517	 * so it is the fallback: a person's later `/reviewer` comment wins over the
518	 * `/engineer` line the body was opened with, which is the whole point.
519	 *
520	 * Read from the SHAPED thread, so a comment the guard is removing does not get to name
521	 * the next agent in the window before it disappears.
522	 *
523	 * Quotations are skipped: the notice preserving a removed comment carries the removed
524	 * text verbatim, and reading a `/agent` line out of it would make the deleted comment
